.TH BNU "1" "2026-08-14" "BNU 9.11" "BNU Commands"
.SH NAME
bnu \- run a BNU core utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bnu
\fI\,COMMAND \/\fR[\fI\,ARG\fR]...
.br
.B bnu
[\fB\-\-help\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
BNU is an independent implementation of the GNU Coreutils 9.11
command\-line interface for the Bun runtime.
.PP
Each utility has an independently runnable entry under
.IR src/commands/ .
The
.B bnu
launcher is retained as a compatibility and discovery surface: its first
operand selects a utility, which is loaded on demand, and the remaining
operands are passed to that utility.  Run
.B bnu \-\-help
to list the implemented commands, or run
.I COMMAND
.B \-\-help
to see command-specific help.
.PP
Command-name wrappers that invoke the single-call entries directly can be
generated with:
.PP
.RS
bun run link\-commands \-\- DIRECTORY
.RE
.PP
For compatibility with the GNU Coreutils multi-call interface, the
.B coreutils
command accepts
.BR \-\-coreutils\-prog= PROGRAM_NAME .
.SH "PLATFORM REQUIREMENTS"
BNU targets Bun on Linux; ordinary ECMAScript support is not sufficient.  All
commands use Bun extensions and Node-compatible APIs.  glibc Linux is the
tested baseline.
.PP
Every command except
.B echo
eagerly loads Bun's
.B bun:ffi
module and
.BR libc.so.6 ,
including for its
.B \-\-help
and
.B \-\-version
paths.  The filename does not by itself require the loaded implementation to
be glibc: another Linux libc exposed under that name can work if it supplies
the complete symbol, calling-convention, layout, and behavior contract.
Command-specific behavior can additionally require Linux
.BR /proc ,
.BR /sys ,
fixed native ABI layouts, inotify, ACL or extended-attribute tools, SELinux or
SMACK, external programs, filesystem support, or elevated privileges.  See
.I docs/runtime-portability.md
in the source distribution for the command and option matrix.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
display the usage and implemented command list, then exit
.TP
.B \-\-version
output BNU version information, then exit
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GNULY_CORRECT
When set to a truthy value such as
.BR 1 ,
emit GNU-compatible diagnostics without BNU's additional
.B Hint:
lines.  An empty value,
.BR 0 ,
or any capitalization of
.B false
leaves friendly hints enabled.  This changes diagnostic wording, not command
semantics.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I bin/bnu.js
compatibility multi-call launcher in a source checkout
.TP
.I src/commands/*.js
independently runnable command entries
.TP
.I src/shared/catalog.js
command inventory and lazy module loader
.TP
.I src/shared/command.js
shared single-call entry behavior
.TP
.I src/shared/runtime.js
compatibility multi-call dispatch
.TP
.I docs/runtime-portability.md
runtime, libc, ABI, kernel, helper-program, and privilege requirements
